.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
.TH OCTA-CAPTURE 1 "" "OCTA-CAPTURE @PROJECT_VERSION@" "OCTA-CAPTURE Manual"
.SH NAME
octa\-capture \- open the OCTA-CAPTURE GTK control panel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBocta-capture\fR [\fB\-\-bin-dir\fR DIR] [\fB\-\-midi-port\fR PORT]
             [\fB\-\-data-dir\fR DIR] [\fB\-\-help\fR]
             [\fB\-\-pair-base\fR ID \fB\-\-pair-expansion\fR ID \fB\-\-experimental-pair\fR]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open the local HTML control panel inside GTK4/WebKitGTK as the regular desktop user.
The Xfce Applications menu lists it under Settings.
The panel controls preamps, compressors, direct mixers, reverb, output routing,
sample rate, Auto-Sens and preset files.
Closing it releases its CTRL connection; independent audio applications continue running.
.PP
At 192 kHz only channels 1 through 4 and Mixer A are available.
The panel reports Linux ALSA information; application/server settings own buffer size.
.PP
The default CTRL MIDI port is hw:CARD=OCTACAPTURE,DEV=0,SUBDEV=1. Close other control-panel/CTRL clients before opening it. Audio streaming is independent of this connection.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-bin-dir DIR
Directory containing the C++ backend programs; installed launchers use their own binary directory.
.TP
.B \-\-midi-port PORT
Select the ALSA raw-MIDI CTRL port.
.TP
.B \-\-data-dir DIR
Private preferences and recovery directory. The default is
$XDG_STATE_HOME/octa-capture, or ~/.local/state/octa-capture.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print options without opening the device.
.SH EXPERIMENTAL PAIRED MODE
Supply all three pair options with distinct serial:SERIAL identities for a
0582:0120 base and 0582:0121 EXP. The panel starts on EXP; the existing device
menu selects either unit and cannot select unrelated devices in this mode.
Both must have coherent 44.1/48/96 kHz clocks, with internal EXP master and active
external base. Connect EXP COAXIAL OUT to base COAXIAL IN and use DIGITAL AUTO
on the base. Missing or changing identities disable paired rate changes.
.PP
EXP rate controls invoke the joint native PulseAudio/clock backend. Base controls
retain the current externally supplied rate. The pair never offers 192 kHz.
Both units must report fresh idle Auto-Sens status; close other CTRL clients so
the companion can be checked. Closing the host cancels lock/helper waits and
waits for restoration; recovery ignores the cancellation flag.
.PP
Linux Audio Settings describes the experimental pair and its total capacity;
capture/playback counts for the selected unit remain separate. This mode does
not install a combined virtual PCM. Use octa-aggregate(1) to prepare that ALSA
configuration, releasing PulseAudio/direct clients before using raw hardware.
Browser/HTTP/backend tests use modeled hardware/audio-server replies; native
WebKit presentation is checked separately. Physical pair streaming, timing and
recovery remain unverified. Normal launches keep single-unit behavior.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success; nonzero indicates a usage, device or operation error.
.SH SEE ALSO
octa-status(1), octa-preset(1), octa-aggregate(1), octa-pair-clock(1)
